# Content & CMS

## Publish switch

```yaml
published: false   # hidden from site, kept in repo
published: true    # public (default)
```

Never delete a piece to "take it offline." Toggle `published` in CMS or front matter.

## Front matter must stay CMS-compatible

Field names in Markdown must match `admin/config.yml` (`title`, `date`, `tags`, `excerpt`, `cover`, `body`, `published`, etc.). Renaming a CMS field without migrating files breaks editing.

## Safe CMS edits

- Do not remove collections or rename `folder:` paths without a migration plan
- Keep `media_folder` / `public_folder` aligned with `assets/uploads`
- `editorial_workflow` is intentional; do not disable unless asked
- Cover paths look like `/assets/uploads/filename.ext`

## Body content

- Write in Markdown (GFM via kramdown)
- Do not paste secrets, private emails of others, or unpublished manuscripts the user did not request to publish
